pattern retry-with-backoff

problem: Retrying external API calls with exponential backoff
solution:
    def retry_with_backoff(ctx: Ctx, operation: str, max_attempts: int) -> Result[T, E]:
        effects: time, net
        for attempt in range(max_attempts):
            result = try_operation(ctx, operation)
            match result:
                case Ok(value):
                    return Ok(value)
                case Err(error):
                    if attempt < max_attempts - 1:
                        backoff_seconds = 2 ** attempt
                        # In real implementation, would sleep here
                        ctx.log.warn(f"Retry {attempt + 1}/{max_attempts} after {backoff_seconds}s")
                    else:
                        return Err(error)
anti-pattern: while True with break
anti-pattern: unbounded loops
anti-pattern: fixed sleep without exponential backoff
